[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]Less Wildlife[/color][/b][/size]

Adjust boar herds and wolf packs from [b]10% to 200%[/b], with a separate switch for each species. [b]100% is the normal population and the default[/b]; 200% doubles the original population.

Only ordinary wild boars and wolves are affected. Quest and named variants, other creatures, health and damage keep their normal values. Positive populations always retain at least one animal.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]

Open [b]Mod Settings > Less Wildlife[/b], choose your settings and press Apply. Population changes take effect on later area encounters.

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Population:[/color][/b] 10% to 200% in 1% steps. Shared by the enabled species; default 100%. Quantities are rounded to the nearest animal.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Adjust boars:[/color][/b] On applies the selected percentage to ordinary boar herds. Off restores original values still controlled by this mod. Default: On.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Adjust wolves:[/color][/b] The same independent choice for ordinary wolf packs. Default: On.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Logging:[/color][/b] Writes aggregated population counts and timings to UE4SS.log. Default: Off.
[/list]

[color=#E6B980]Off disables population scaling for that species; it does not remove the animals.[/color] Already spawned animals are unaffected. Setting Population to 100% also restores original values still controlled by this mod. Changes made by the game or another mod are preserved.

[size=3][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual configuration[/color][/b][/size]

Launch the game once to create settings.ini, then close it. Open this file inside your The Blood of Dawnwalker game folder:

[code]Dawnwalker\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\LessWildlife\settings.ini[/code]

[code][LessWildlife]
populationPercent = 100
reduceBoars = 1
reduceWolves = 1
debugLogging = 0[/code]

Use an integer from 10 to 200 for populationPercent. For the switches, use 0 for Off or 1 for On. Save and restart the game. Missing species-switch keys default to On.

Unusually large areas or very dense bursts of encounters keep their current population values until a later encounter can be handled.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install Less-Wildlife.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy the archive's Data/LessWildlife folder into <The Blood of Dawnwalker>/Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods, preserving the folder structure.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Credits and source[/color][/b][/size]

Inspired by [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/326]Less Boars[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/318]Less Wolves[/url] by MrSecondPlayer, including their 40% preset and ordinary-species selection. This custom implementation does not include the original scripts or artwork.

Thanks to the UE4SS contributors and to mmarcussa for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Mod Setting Menu[/url] and its unchanged integration helper, included under the guide's copying permission.

Banner and thumbnail are AI-enhanced from [url=https://open.video/@jasonsvideogamessource-com/v/the-blood-of-dawnwalker-prologue-fist-fight-stance-fight-boars-with-fists-unblockable-attacks]gameplay by Jason's Video Games Source[/url], used under the creator's stated reuse permission with credit. HUD removed and title added. Reconstructed details may differ from the original game frame. Promotional artwork, not a before-and-after comparison.

